{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>These are the people of the province</b> — In the preceding verse he said \"to register.\" The meaning: to show the genealogy, and he found written in it: \"These are the people of the province who went up.\" And when the wall of Jerusalem was joined, Nehemiah wanted them to be registered by their ancestral houses so that strangers would not intermingle with them. Many were added who are not in the first count, and many diminished, who had already died and were not in the days of Nehemiah, and many had fathered sons during the thirty-six years — two under Cyrus and fourteen under Ahasuerus and twenty under Artaxerxes — until Nehemiah's arrival; and concerning those found, he said \"to register.\" And if one asks: Why did he say, \"written in it: These are the people of the province who went up,\" yet they are not in the first count, and there are some in the first who are not in the second? For in the first he said: the sons of Arah 965, and in the second the sons of Arah 652 — the former exceeded by 313. The sons of Senaah: in the first 3,000 and 730, and in the second 3,000 and 930 — and the second exceeded. And there are those mentioned in the first who are not mentioned in the second, such as the sons of Jorah 112 and the sons of Bani-Chariph 112. We answer him: The verse speaks in accordance with the majority. It says, \"to kill the seventy sons of Jerubbaal,\" yet Jotham was not killed; and likewise \"those who came out of Jacob's thigh, seventy,\" yet Jacob did not come out of his thigh, being seventy. Or perhaps Jorah and Chariph are two names for one man, like Seraiah, Reelaiah, and in the second Azariah, Raamiah. And the second count is slightly larger than the first. Only in saying \"these who went up\" — to make known that the sons of so-and-so were not diminished, not one of them, and the sons of so-and-so were added, and the sons of so-and-so were diminished and some of them died. And I have already explained the whole matter above."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:25.883389318Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}